From ac5146c5f5fc45b333b9940646bf11f5836dc7c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 16:16:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] bluetooth: dynamically load the ARC bridge
 (libbluetooth_arc) instead of Fluoride
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The AOSP-13 Fluoride stack needs an IBluetoothHci HAL, which the ARC container
doesn't have (it bridges Bluetooth to the host BlueZ at the bt_interface_t level
via libbluetooth_arc, a Mojo bridge). Statically-linked Fluoride therefore
crash-loops com.android.bluetooth (no HCI; also the CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM issue).

Build libbluetooth_jni with -DDYNAMIC_LOAD_BLUETOOTH so hal_util_load_bt_library
dlopen()s the bt_interface_t at runtime, and point that dlopen at
libbluetooth_arc.so directly (instead of "libbluetooth.so") — avoids renaming the
ARC lib or colliding with the statically-linked Fluoride libbluetooth, and keeps
it at /system/lib64. (Pairs with a system/linkerconfig change letting the
com.android.btservices apex namespace load libbluetooth_arc + its ARC-bridge deps
from /system.)

Verified on device: libbluetooth_jni dlopens libbluetooth_arc; the bridge
logs "ARC bridge ready / registered BluetoothInstance with Chrome OS /
BluetoothHost connected". Fluoride is bypassed (HCI/timerfd crashes gone).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Id3d580533b98c141a08911042b203aad02e08ec1
---
 android/app/Android.bp                                      | 5 +++++
 .../jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp  | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/app/Android.bp b/android/app/Android.bp
index 2e71dccc46..d5eb9dc914 100644
--- a/android/app/Android.bp
+++ b/android/app/Android.bp
@@ -57,6 +57,11 @@ cc_library_shared {
     name: "libbluetooth_jni",
     defaults: ["fluoride_full_defaults"],
     srcs: ["jni/**/*.cpp"],
+    // fydroid/ARC: load the bt_interface_t at runtime via dlopen("libbluetooth.so")
+    // + dlsym("bluetoothInterface") instead of the statically-linked Fluoride one,
+    // so the ARC Mojo bridge (libbluetooth_arc, deployed as libbluetooth.so) can
+    // replace the Fluoride stack (which has no HCI HAL in the container).
+    cflags: ["-DDYNAMIC_LOAD_BLUETOOTH"],
     header_libs: [
         "jni_headers",
         "libbluetooth_headers",
diff --git a/android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp b/android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp
index f25e208d97..270d2e49ef 100644
--- a/android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp
+++ b/android/app/jni/com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterService.cpp
@@ -886,8 +886,10 @@ int hal_util_load_bt_library(const bt_interface_t** interface) {
   const char* sym = BLUETOOTH_INTERFACE_STRING;
   bt_interface_t* itf = nullptr;
 
-  // The library name is not set by default, so the preset library name is used.
-  void* handle = dlopen("libbluetooth.so", RTLD_NOW);
+  // fydroid/ARC: load the ARC Mojo bridge (libbluetooth_arc) directly by its own
+  // name instead of "libbluetooth.so" — avoids renaming it / colliding with the
+  // statically-linked Fluoride libbluetooth, and keeps it at /system/lib64.
+  void* handle = dlopen("libbluetooth_arc.so", RTLD_NOW);
   if (!handle) {
     const char* err_str = dlerror();
     ALOGE("%s: failed to load Bluetooth library, error=%s", __func__,
-- 
